(CVE-2026-91733)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Google Chrome: Cross-origin data disclosure due to uninitialized resource in Skia (CVE-2026-91740)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: chromium-browser: Uninitialized resource in Skia (CVE-2026-102325)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Integer overflow in Skia (CVE-2026-103629)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Uninitialized resource in Skia (CVE-2026-106379)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Out of bounds read in Skia (CVE-2026-106399)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Memory corruption in Skia (CVE-2026-113106)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Improper input validation in Skia (CVE-2026-118348)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Memory corruption in Skia (CVE-2026-118351)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Memory corruption in Skia (CVE-2026-118340)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Improper input validation in Skia (CVE-2026-118354)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Memory corruption in Skia (CVE-2026-118319)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Use after free in Skia (CVE-2026-119271)\n  * chromium-browser: skia: Improper input validation in Skia (CVE-2026-119261)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * webkit2gtk3 2.54.0 regression breaks Eclipse IDE WebKit-based views on CentOS Stream 9 (JIRA:RHEL-271317)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
